Understanding Vault Architecture
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the core components of HashiCorp Vault architecture
Explore Vault Server components and their functions
Configure and work with different Storage Backends
Implement and manage various Secrets Engines
Analyze how Vault components interact within the overall architecture
Demonstrate practical knowledge of Vault's structural design
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with text editors (nano, vim, or similar)
Basic knowledge of JSON and YAML formats
Understanding of basic security concepts
Completion of Lab 1 or equivalent Vault installation experience
